<title>FRANCE: French stocks back in the black after U.S. data.</title>
<headline>French stocks back in the black after U.S. data.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shares were back into the black after the publication of U.S. jobless claims and international trade data, dealers said.</p>
<p>The blue-chip CAC-40 index was up 3.59 points or 0.14 percent at 2,624.56 at 1234 GMT while the CAC-40 futures contract was up eight at 2,260.</p>
<p>Volume was 3.3 billion francs.</p>
</text>
